      "value": "q0_pay_when_roi_clear",
      "rationale": "As a busy dual-income parent, I'm willing to pay once I see clear value in reducing calendar fragmentation and stress. The free tier lets me test if it actually solves our family's coordination chaos before committing.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q1",
      "value": "q1_plus_after_sustained_use",
      "rationale": "Plus ($6.99) covers my core need—up to 6 family members and weekly digests. Pro's email parsing is nice but not essential. I'd upgrade to Plus once I confirm sustained daily use, then evaluate Pro later if needed.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q2",
      "value": "q2_annual_after_long_use",
      "rationale": "I prefer monthly flexibility early on—family needs change, and I don't want to be locked into annual prepay before proving the app fits our rhythm. After 3–6 months of real use, I'd consider annual to save money.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q3",
      "value": "q3_one_dollar_try_cancel",
      "rationale": "A $1 first month is low-friction enough to test Plus features without guilt. I'd cancel immediately if the digest and handoffs don't noticeably reduce our family stress and missed deadlines.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q4",
      "value": "q4_compare_pay_if_wins",
      "rationale": "I'm not dogmatic about free vs. paid. If a friend's app genuinely solves the fragmentation problem better than FocusLoop, I'd pay for it—but only after comparing features and confirming it's worth the switch cost.",
      "confidence": 0.83
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q5",
      "value": "q5_ads_pay_if_plus_useful",
      "rationale": "Ads on free tier are tolerable, but I wouldn't upgrade *just* to remove them. If Plus delivers real organizational value (digests, handoffs, more members), I'll happily pay and ads disappearing is a bonus.",
      "confidence": 0.81
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q6",
      "value": "q6_fair_if_use_justifies",
      "rationale": "At $6.99–$11.99/month, FocusLoop is reasonably priced for a family coordination tool. It's fair if daily use genuinely cuts down stress, missed appointments, and group chat chaos. If it doesn't, I'll stay free.",
      "confidence": 0.84
    },
    {
      "questionId": "overall_interest",
      "value": 4,
      "rationale": "Very interested—this directly addresses a real pain point in our household. The calm weekly view and task handoffs appeal to me, though I need to see it work in practice before full enthusiasm.",
